   }
  ]
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "A regular local ring of dimension one has\n$\\dim_R\\mathfrak m/\\mathfrak m^2=1$, so $\\mathfrak m=(t)$ for\nsome $t$ (Nakayama's lemma: *reference: Stacks Project,\nAlgebra, Lemma 10.20.1, [Tag 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV)*), and $R$ is a domain\n([lem-sc-regular-local-domain]). Hence $R$ is a discrete\nvaluation ring by [lem-sc-principal-ideal-dvr].",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-regular-local-domain",
    "lem-sc-principal-ideal-dvr"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
